  "id": "scapular-protraction",
  "name": "Scapular Protraction",
  "definition": "A strict open-chain scapular isolation whose concentric phase moves one scapula anterolaterally around the thorax while the humerus remains held at 90 degrees of forward elevation and the elbow remains extended. The initial contract admits only the directly reviewed supine dumbbell scapular punch. It does not infer a pure translation from serratus-anterior EMG: the source prescribes full available protraction through a loaded range, while the family forbids dynamic shoulder and elbow motion. Push-up-plus, dynamic-hug, cable-punch, wall-slide, bodyweight, bilateral, standing, and overhead variants remain outside this narrow contract until their coupled glenohumeral and scapular rotations are reviewed directly.",
  "evidenceRefs": [
    "castelein-2016-serratus-pectoralis-minor-protraction",
    "intelangelo-2022-supine-scapular-punch",
    "seth-2019-shoulder-work"
